From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 12:40:23 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] usb: musb: mediatek: run the MT6797 USB11 controller as
 multipoint

On a Gemini PDA's right USB-C port every device connects and then fails
its first control transfer with -EPROTO, at full and at high speed, with
a PHY that now reads the same as under the vendor kernel. The vendor
kernel's musbfsh enumerates the same keyboard.

The MT6797 USB11 data copied multipoint = false from the vendor
configuration, but the vendor core sets is_multipoint = 1 regardless
and addresses targets through the per-endpoint function address
registers at 0x480, as this glue's busctl_offset does for the other
MediaTek controllers. Without multipoint the MUSB core writes FADDR and
programs no target speed, and the controller reaches no device. It also
warned that external hubs must be disabled.

Set multipoint for the USB11 controller.
---
 drivers/usb/musb/mediatek.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/musb/mediatek.c b/drivers/usb/musb/mediatek.c
index 9b0cab801..2cf17c8df 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/musb/mediatek.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/musb/mediatek.c
@@ -417,7 +417,12 @@ static const struct musb_fifo_cfg mt6797_usb11_mode_cfg[] = {
 static const struct musb_hdrc_config mt6797_usb11_hdrc_config = {
 	.fifo_cfg = mt6797_usb11_mode_cfg,
 	.fifo_cfg_size = ARRAY_SIZE(mt6797_usb11_mode_cfg),
-	.multipoint = false,
+	/*
+	 * Like the other MediaTek MUSBs, the USB11 controller addresses targets
+	 * through the per-endpoint function address registers. The vendor
+	 * driver's configuration says false but its core forces multipoint.
+	 */
+	.multipoint = true,
 	.dyn_fifo = true,
 	.num_eps = 6,
 	.ram_bits = MTK_MUSB_RAM_BITS,
-- 
